🎯 Exam Focus

For theory questions, especially remember:

Normalization vs Standardization →
Normalization uses minimum and maximum, while standardization uses mean and standard deviation.

Discrete vs Continuous →
Discrete values are countable; continuous values can take any value within a range.

Population vs Sample →
Population = entire group; Sample = subset of the population.

Descriptive vs Inferential Statistics →
Descriptive statistics summarize data; inferential statistics use sample data to make conclusions about a population.

CLT →
When sample size is sufficiently large, the sampling distribution of the sample mean tends to become approximately normal, under its usual conditions.